    [Test] Port Kimi K3 MRV2 coverage and DeepSeek weekly scheduling to main (#20195)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Port #19774 from `releases/v0.30.0` to `main` by cherry-picking merged
    commit `c18dc97856708359e3e6546a22a319c5e03c540d` with `-x -s`. The
    cherry-pick applies without conflicts and preserves source attribution.
    
    - Add Kimi K3 MRV2 four-card E2E coverage using shared reduced-model
    builders and scenario helpers, including a plain generation smoke test.
    - Register the four-node A3 nightly case (DP4 / TP16 / EP64), model
    dataset entry, and test scheduling estimate.
    - Enable D-Spark with the MLA NPU draft checkpoint, seven speculative
    tokens, draft TP16, greedy sampling, safetensors prefetch, and
    FULL_DECODE_ONLY graph capture sizes 16/32/64/128/256. Set max-num-seqs
    to 32 and GPQA output to 24576 tokens; retain the accuracy and
    performance thresholds from #19774.
    - Move DeepSeek-V4-Pro-w4a8-1M-PD from nightly to weekly, preserving its
    configuration and four-node allocation.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. Changes are limited to tests and CI configuration; no release note
    fragment is required. The draft checkpoint
    `/root/.cache/modelscope/hub/models/Eco-Tech/Kimi-K3-DSpark-MLA-NPU`
    must be available in all four nightly containers.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Parsed all seven changed files with Python AST, PyYAML, or JSON as
    appropriate.
    - Checked that every imported Kimi test helper exists in the shared
    module.
    - Verified that Kimi MRV2 appears once in nightly, DeepSeek 1M is absent
    from nightly and appears once in weekly, and both scheduled cases
    resolve to existing configuration files with four-node allocations.
    - Tokenized all four deployment commands and parsed their JSON
    configuration. Verified ranks 0-3, max-num-seqs=32, prefetch, D-Spark
    with seven speculative tokens and draft TP16 matching target TP16,
    enforce_eager=false, explicit graph capture sizes, and the GPQA output
    cap.
    - `git diff upstream/main HEAD --check` passed.
    - Full `bash format.sh ci` could not run because Bash is unavailable in
    this Windows environment. Ruff is also unavailable. Full lint remains
    for CI.
    - NPU E2E and four-node nightly execution were not run locally. Hardware
    compatibility, model availability, and configured benchmark thresholds
    still require CI validation.
    
    ### Checklist
    
    - [ ] Boundary / edge-case coverage: existing scenario coverage is
    reused; hardware execution remains pending.
    - [ ] Regression test: this ports test coverage and scheduling rather
    than a runtime bug fix.
    - [ ] Error / failure path coverage: no new error handling is
    introduced.
    - [x] Meaningful & reliable tests: reused tests assert model execution
    behavior; the additional smoke test exercises plain generation.
    - [ ] Performance impact: no runtime implementation changes; configured
    performance benchmarks have not been run locally.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
